                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Most likely, a second half of the nineteenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Fine, regular. The name of the scribe, now unreadable, was mentioned in the subscriptio under <ref target="#ms_i1.5.4"/>.</desc> 
                        <note>It is unclear whether the scribe who wrote the text of <ref target="#q1"/> is the same person as that behind <ref target="#h1"/>.</note>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Headings and incipits of the texts; a few lines on the incipit page of the introduction and of each Gospel (alternating with black
                           lines); numbers of the ‘tituli’; chapter numbers and the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">‘mǝʿrāf’</foreign>;
                           headings of sections; grid lines of the canon tables; headings and postscripts of the canons; elements of punctuation marks; elements of Ethiopic numerals.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  
